Commit:     GitHub <noreply@github.com>
CommitDate: Tue Oct 13 19:13:16 2026 +0800

    [BugFix][CI] Update image dependencies (#18578)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    Release image builds currently use the older CANN base image and skip
    snapshot dependency installation. This PR updates the Dockerfile
    defaults and workflow arguments to use the following dependency
    snapshots for v0.30.0rc2:
    
    | Dependency | Version | Build |
    | --- | --- | --- |
    | CANN | 9.2.0 | 20260930220649 |
    | memcache | 1.3.0 | 20261009.15 |
    | memfabric | 1.3.0 | 20261009.10 |
    | torch_npu bundle | 26.2.0 | 20260926.5 |
    | triton-ascend | 3.6.0+dev20260923230212 | 20260923230212 |
    
    - Pin the dependency defaults in all eight Dockerfiles.
    - Enable snapshot dependency installation for both release and daily
    builds.
    - Align workflow defaults and fallback arguments with the Dockerfiles.
    - Preserve release image tags and publishing destinations.
    - Keep the existing torch_npu-only installation mode for 310P.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    Yes. Release images use the updated dependency snapshots. Users building
    from the rc2 source can run `docker build .` without supplying
    dependency-related build arguments.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/ced6857afa0ea7b2e3f0846a62e1394e90f15607
    
    Signed-off-by: MrZ20 <2609716663@qq.com>

